From cf00b4911d26314b6cc41e29ba90e6c7aed0941d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaxorcist <vaxorcist@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:45:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DMV11/DMP11: DMP/DMV host interface, multipoint, DMP on
 Unibus VAXen

The DMV11 work as one commit (version 11: the DMV11 on the MicroVAX I,
pdp11_dmc.c in the Visual Studio .vcxproj files; version 10: the control station polls its
tributaries; version 9: multipoint select flag discipline at the control
station; version 8: the DMP11 is the DMP device on every Unibus
simulator; no SET DROPS, a listening station instead; up to 32
tributaries on the DMP11).

Host interface (DMP11 on the Unibus, DMV11 on the Qbus):
- The DMV device in the MicroVAX I, MicroVAX II and MicroVAX 3900
  simulators and the PDP-11, the DMP device in the Unibus VAX simulators (VAX-11/730, 750,
  780, VAX 8200, 8600) and the PDP-11; DMP and DMV share one DIB, sized
  per device in dmc_reset.  The DMV11 auto-configuration entry gets its
  device name.
- Fix dmc_get_controller_from_address (unit offset) so register
  accesses reach the right controller.
- DMP/DMV command set: mode definition, control commands
  (establish/delete/start/maintenance/halt tributary, modem read/write,
  GSS/TSS read, read-and-clear and write), receive and transmit buffers
  in 18-bit and Q22 formats, master-clear signature.
- Output codes of Table 3-7 (EK-DMV11-TM-001): 004 transmit threshold,
  010/012/014 protocol events, 024 run, 0100-0140 procedural errors,
  0300 buffer too small, 0302 NXM, 0304 disconnect, 0306 overflow.
- Status memory access rules (Table 3-5), TSS/GSS parameter defaults
  (Tables 4-2, 4-3) and TSS counters.
- Control command BSEL7: common receive pool with quota, errors 134 and
  140; latch/unlatch accepted.
- Halt returns the tributary's buffers (types 3, 6, 7), then information
  response 020; global halt returns the common pool buffers (error 136
  while the pool is in use).  010/012 return buffers too.

Multipoint (control station and tributary station):
- Every established tributary gets its own DDCMP session; messages are
  routed by the tributary address in the header.
- Receive buffers for tributary 0 form the common pool (manual 4.6.2.2).
- A DMP11 or DMV11 line attached without a PEER listens on its port for
  as many stations as the controller has tributaries; a multipoint
  control station uses every connection as a drop line, any other
  station the first connection it gets.  Per-tributary SHOW DDCMP.
- Tributary limit (tributary status slots): DMP11 32, DMV11 12; ESTABLISH
  beyond it is procedural error 114.
- A lost drop line is not a modem disconnect at the control station;
  304 is sent once per outage.
- DDCMP sequence number window no longer tied to the buffer pool size.
- Select flag discipline at the control station: a selected tributary
  owns the line until it sends a message with the select flag; meanwhile
  the messages to it go out without the select flag.  A selection timer
  (10 s) takes the line back.  A tributary running DDCMP in software
  (DMF32 under VMS V3.5) otherwise answered every extra select with a REP
  and restarted the line ("Line synchronization lost") when a new
  logical link came in.
- Polling: the control station selects an idle tributary that has
  returned the line (an ACK with the select flag) after 0.5 s.  Such a
  tributary may only transmit when selected; without polling its routing
  hellos could only follow the control station's own, and every couple
  of hours the control station's listen timer expired ("adjacency down,
  listener receive timeout").

Device options and help: SET DMVn CORRUPTION as on the DMP; the DMP and
DMV connection poll interval defaults to 2 seconds like the DMC's (it was
0, shown as such); the help text is put together per device (SET TYPE
only for the DMC device, multipoint only for DMP and DMV) and describes
the listening station.

MicroVAX I (KA610): DMV11 interrupts in vax610_defs.h; same address,
vector and master-clear self-test signature as on the MicroVAX II.  Build
files: makefile, CMake and Visual Studio (.vcproj, .vcxproj, .filters)
for the MicroVAX I, II and 3900.

Tested with VMS V4.7 (MicroVAX II DMV11, VAX-11/780 DMP11) and VMS V3.7
(VAX-11/780 DMP11, DMP device): DECnet start-up, SET HOST, remote copy +
DIFFERENCES = 0, circuit restart, transmit threshold recovery; three-node
multipoint (control station listening without a PEER, tributaries 2 and
3) with routing, copies and circuit off/on of one tributary on the
VAX-11/780 (DMP11) and the MicroVAX II (DMV11); point-to-point with a
listening station, also with SET DMV0 CORRUPTION=5; tributary limit 12
(DMV11) and 32 (DMP11).  Multipoint with a software DDCMP
tributary: VAX-11/730 with DMF32 under VMS V3.5 as tributary 4 of a
VAX-11/780 DMP11 control station (VMS V4.7): node hopping with SET HOST
(10 rounds, no circuit restart) and remote copies; idle line with the
tributary's hello timer at 25 s (control station 15 s, listen timer 30
s): no adjacency loss in 10 minutes with polling, a loss without.

